WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
The Oscars really want us.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.254
I'm trying to keep it together.

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:06.506
I'm like, you gotta,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.757
you,

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:08.341
huh?

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.219
(soft piano music)

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:16.433
- I was driving in rush
hour traffic on the 101,

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:18.059
and I got a call.

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:19.477
- Well, Packer actually
called us and said,

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:22.272
"Hey, like you're about to
actually present trophies

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:23.106
"at The Academy."

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:24.941
And I was like, oh, snap.

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:27.360
- And basically they're
looking into you and Josh

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.446
to be presenters at the Oscars.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.114
I was like,

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:32.407
(woman laughing)

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.242
I was like, "Stop lying,
I have to finish packing."

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:35.493
Like, "What are you talking about?"

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:36.619
- I'm like, "Oh, she's serious."

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:39.539
Like, so the Oscars really want us.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.332
I'm trying to keep it together.

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:43.585
I'm like, you gotta,

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:44.836
you,

00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:45.670
huh?

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.757
- And I finally got off on
an exit and I pulled over

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.091
and, again, I tried to play it cool.

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:51.801
I was like, "Yeah, no, it's totally fine."

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.053
But I was like, "What
the hell's happening?"

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:55.513
And people like driving by
me and going around me and.

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:57.974
- It feels like it's a dream.

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:00.560
It feels like it's not actually real

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.687
or that I'm gonna wake up at some point.

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:05.940
- You know, once you guys
actually explained, you know,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.860
what a trophy presenter
was, then I was like, oh,

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.696
so like you get to go on
stage and actually, you know,

00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:13.031
give the trophies to the people.

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:16.242
- I've been to many an award ceremony,

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.412
but this is the mother
of all award ceremonies.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.915
So I'm excited to just be present

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.541
and just sort of like take it all in.

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:26.377
- To have the opportunity to
just be in the same presence

00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:30.381
of the people I look up
to, like role models,

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:32.425
being able to just see them.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.094
- On the professor side, it's very cool,

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.679
'cause I get to watch how
things are put together.

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:38.515
It's information I can
share with my students.

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:40.600
It has an upside on that,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.684
'cause at the end of the day,

00:01:41.684 --> 00:01:43.895
the only reason I'll
mention this to students

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:45.814
is to help them make something, I think.

00:01:45.814 --> 00:01:47.732
- I think that it's gonna
be exciting for my students

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:50.944
to just, at the very least,
and especially, you know,

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.320
my marginalized students,

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.281
to see somebody up there
and have a direct connection

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.200
to something that's felt so mystical

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.577
and so far out of reach.

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:02.413
- I watched the Oscars growing up.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.666
In the past couple of years,

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:08.586
a lot of Mexican directors
have been nominated

00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:10.213
and awarded in the Oscars,

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:15.218
and it's really such an honor
watching them be on stage.

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:19.180
And just seeing myself
with that possibility

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.057
of being on that stage, as well.

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:22.976
- I think now more than ever,

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:26.688
this is the most inclusion
that I've seen at the Oscars,

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:27.897
and I'm loving it.

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:30.733
- This was just a blessing to
be able to go to the Oscars,

00:02:30.733 --> 00:02:31.985
but let alone go Oscars

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.279
by actually presenting
awards, present trophies

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:35.572
to people that are in
the movies that I watch

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.574
and for the people I look up to.

